---
import Charter from "../../layouts/Charter.astro";
import Article from "../../components/Article.astro";
import art from "../../../assets/plates/panel-progression.png";
import { DISCORD_INVITE } from "../../config";

const articles = [
  { id: "who-we-are", title: "Who we are" },
  { id: "who-can-use-it", title: "Who can use it" },
  { id: "your-account", title: "Your account" },
  { id: "conduct", title: "Conduct" },
  { id: "what-you-post", title: "What you post" },
  { id: "addons", title: "Addons and links" },
  { id: "other-services", title: "Other services" },
  { id: "no-guarantees", title: "No guarantees" },
  { id: "ending", title: "Leaving, or being removed" },
  { id: "changes", title: "Changes and questions" },
];
---

<Charter
  title="Terms of service · SideQuest"
  description="The terms for using SideQuest's guild site: who it's for, what you post, and what it promises."
  heading="TERMS OF SERVICE"
  lede="The agreement between you and SideQuest when you use this site, kept as short as we could make it."
  effective="October 28, 2026"
  art={art}
  artPosition="78% 45%"
  articles={articles}
>
  <Article id="who-we-are" n={1} title="Who we are">
    <p>
      SideQuest is a player-run guild on World of Warcraft: Forever. Guild officers run this site for free, as a hobby,
      so members can sign up for events and find the guild's addons. By using it you agree to these terms, the{" "}
      <a href="/rules/">Guild rules</a> and the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> page.
    </p>
    <p>
      We're not affiliated with or endorsed by Blizzard Entertainment or Discord. World of Warcraft is a trademark of
      Blizzard Entertainment, Inc.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="who-can-use-it" n={2} title="Who can use it">
    <p class="charter-mark">You must be 18 or older to sign in or take part.</p>
    <p>
      Anyone can read the public pages. Signing up for events needs a Discord account and membership in the SideQuest
      Discord.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="your-account" n={3} title="Your account">
    <p>
      You sign in with Discord, so your account is only as safe as your Discord account. Officer access comes from
      officer roles in the SideQuest Discord, and losing the role removes the access.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="conduct" n={4} title="Conduct">
    <p>
      The <a href="/rules/">Guild rules</a> apply here too: in character names, notes and everything else you enter.
      Don't try to break, overload or get around the site's sign-in or officer checks.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="what-you-post" n={5} title="What you post">
    <p>
      Your sign-ups and notes stay yours. By posting them you let the guild show them on the site and in Discord so
      events can run. Officers may edit or remove anything that breaks the rules.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="addons" n={6} title="Addons and links">
    <p>
      Addon links point to files hosted elsewhere. Install them at your own risk, keep backups of your settings, and
      only use addons that Blizzard's rules allow.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="other-services" n={7} title="Other services">
    <p>
      Discord, Battle.net and World of Warcraft have their own terms, and you agreed to those with them, not with us.
      Nothing here changes them.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="no-guarantees" n={8} title="No guarantees">
    <p>
      The site is provided as it is, with no warranty of any kind. It may change, go down or shut down at any time. To
      the fullest extent the law allows, SideQuest and its officers aren't liable for any loss that comes from using it,
      missed raid nights and lost loot included.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="ending" n={9} title="Leaving, or being removed">
    <p>
      You can delete your account at any time on your <a href="/account/">Account</a> page. Officers may suspend or
      remove access for anyone who breaks these terms or the Guild rules.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="changes" n={10} title="Changes and questions">
    <p>
      When these terms change, this page and its date change with them. Significant changes are announced in the Discord
      first, and using the site afterwards means you accept them. Questions go to an officer in the{" "}
      <a href={DISCORD_INVITE}>SideQuest Discord</a>.
    </p>
  </Article>
</Charter>
